Feature: The bars of the app
  The top bar shows the clock, the score of each team and a chip for each tower, in the colour
  of the team that holds it. The bottom bar has the minimap at the left, a card for each of your
  drones in the middle, and the command card at the right.

  The card of each drone shows the order that the server has for the drone, its altitude, and
  the picture from its camera. This picture is the same [[sensor feed]] that the ground station
  shows. Click a picture to select its drone.

  When one drone is selected, the bottom bar shows its PORTRAIT and its UNIT panel. The
  PORTRAIT is a large picture from the camera of the drone. The UNIT panel shows a small icon of
  the drone and its basic numbers: its class, its weight on a tower, its mass, its speed, its
  altitude and its state. The icon is a quadcopter for a light drone, and a plane for a standard
  or a heavy drone.

  Expectation: The top bar shows the towers that each team holds
    At the start, each team holds its home tower.

    When the commander joins the game
    Then the towers held by Blue in the top bar are 1

  Expectation: With no drone selected, there is no UNIT panel
    Given the selected drone is none
    Then the unit panel of the app is hidden

  Expectation: The UNIT panel shows the details of the selected drone
    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    Then the unit panel of the app is shown
    And the class in the unit panel is standard
    And the mass in the unit panel is 1.1 kg

  Expectation: The card of each drone shows its camera
    The pictures come when the 3D view has loaded the valley. That takes some minutes after a
    game starts, and the game goes on meanwhile.

    When the commander waits for the cameras
    Then the camera feeds in the app are 5

  Expectation: The PORTRAIT shows the camera of the selected drone
    The pictures come when the 3D view has loaded the valley.

    Given the selected drone is the first Blue drone
    When the commander waits for the cameras
    Then the picture in the portrait is the camera of the first Blue drone

  Expectation: With no drone selected, there is no PORTRAIT
    Given the selected drone is none
    Then the picture in the portrait is nothing

  Expectation: A click on a camera selects its drone
    When the commander clicks the camera of the second Blue drone
    Then the selected drone is the second Blue drone
